# Build output
# `build*` rather than `build/` and `build-*/`: a directory named
# build142 matched neither, and a stray one was committed-adjacent long
# enough to notice. Nothing tracked begins with `build`.
build*/
build/
build-*/
build-sketch/
*.o
*.a
*.elf
*.bin
*.hex
*.map
*.lst
*.su

# CMake
CMakeCache.txt
CMakeFiles/
cmake_install.cmake
compile_commands.json

# arduino-cli
sketches/**/build/
*.ino.bin
*.ino.elf
*.ino.map

# Vendored toolchains / SDKs (fetched, not committed)
tools/toolchain/
tools/arm-gnu-toolchain-*/
tools/xpack-*/

# Host tooling
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/

# Captures and scratch data
captures/
*.npy
*.raw

# macOS
.DS_Store
.venv-gui/
.venv-ft/

# Per-machine tool locations (the shared registry is toolchains.json)
toolchains.local.json

# Calibration output. Written by --calibrate for a human to promote
# into baseline.json, never to be committed as it is.
tests/baseline.measured.json

# Phase 0 summaries. Derived from the .jsonl records beside them by
# `tools/phase0.py --report`, and a derived file in the tree is a second
# home for a number that already has one.
records/*.summary.json

# A bench declares its own cabling; see host/provenance.py. One desk,
# not the repository.
bench.json

# The flash log is one desk's history of what it put on its board.
records/flash-log.jsonl
build-c/
records/issue35-reflash-transcripts.log

# Agent worktrees: transient copies of the whole tree. Source-scanning
# guards (tests/test_clean_build.py) otherwise see one "second build path"
# per live agent.
.claude/worktrees/

# Core dumps. A crashing native harness drops `core` in the working
# directory, and under an emulated ABI the emulator drops its own -
# qemu-i386 wrote 101 MB of them here in one container run, which then
# appear in every other agent's `git status` as untracked source.
#
# `core.<pid>` is the third form and it was missing: WSL2's
# kernel.core_pattern is the bare string `core`, so the kernel appends
# the pid and the dump lands as `core.1234`, which neither `core` nor
# `*.core` matches. Three 39 MB dumps then made the tree dirty in the
# middle of a container run, on a bench where `FW_GIT_REV` picks the
# dirt up and bakes it into the image.
core
core.*
*.core
